---
source: crates/cache-explorer-core/tests/golden.rs
description: "A 16 B cache of one 16 B line: fully associative with one way, so the decode names no set and the victim line does not say direct-mapped (cases 2, 1 and 3)."
---
1.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Load 0x0A4: tag 0x0A, offset 4 (word 1). Fully associative: one set, no index bits.
1.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, loads, misses | - | Set 0 is invalid. Miss.
1.3 | victim | associativity | - | - | Set 0 has one way; the line goes there.
1.4 | fill | lineSize | valid 0/0, tag 0/0, word 0/0/0, word 0/0/1, word 0/0/2, word 0/0/3, fills | - | Fill way 0 with line 0x0A0–0x0AF from memory.
1.5 | complete | - | r1 | - | Read word 1 of way 0 (53) into r1.
2.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Load 0x0A8: tag 0x0A, offset 8 (word 2). Fully associative: one set, no index bits.
2.2 | hit | associativity | accesses, loads, hits | - | Set 0, way 0: valid, and tag 0x0A matches. Hit.
2.3 | complete | - | r1 | - | Read word 2 of way 0 (66) into r1.
3.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Load 0x1A4: tag 0x1A, offset 4 (word 1). Fully associative: one set, no index bits.
3.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, loads, misses | - | Set 0 holds tag 0x0A, not 0x1A. Miss.
3.3 | victim | associativity | - | - | Way 0 is the only place for this line, so its current line must go.
3.4 | evict | associativity | valid 0/0, tag 0/0, word 0/0/0, word 0/0/1, word 0/0/2, word 0/0/3, evictions | - | Evict line 0x0A0 (tag 0x0A) from way 0.
3.5 | fill | lineSize | valid 0/0, tag 0/0, word 0/0/0, word 0/0/1, word 0/0/2, word 0/0/3, fills | - | Fill way 0 with line 0x1A0–0x1AF from memory.
3.6 | complete | - | r1 | - | Read word 1 of way 0 (12) into r1.
